# The entire fixture corpus — real production scripts, hand-written
# structural-shape fixtures, their golden formatted counterparts, and the
# deliberately-malformed encoding fixtures — is byte-exactness-sensitive:
# format()/format_bytes() (002-cli-check-format, FR-012) deliberately
# preserves each line's original line-ending style rather than normalizing
# it, so a golden-file comparison against `git`-mangled line endings is
# spurious, not a real drift. Discovered the hard way: the narrower rules
# below (originally scoped to just real_corpus/ and encoding_fallback/) left
# tests/fixtures/golden/'s hand-written-fixture counterparts unprotected,
# and core.autocrlf=true silently rewrote them to CRLF on a fresh checkout
# (the 002-cli-check-format -> main fast-forward merge), failing
# hand_written_fixtures_match_golden_output even though nothing about the
# actual formatter had changed. One broad rule for the whole tree closes
# this permanently rather than requiring a new carve-out every time a new
# fixture subdirectory is added.
crates/voyager-core/tests/fixtures/** -text
